\title{Extraction reaches 27 of 96 single-precision entrypoints and no other}
\taxon{Problem}
\date{2026-11-23}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{extraction}
\tag{survey}
\meta{status}{open}
\meta{created}{2026-11-23}
\meta{pr}{6}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\strong{Status:} open.}
\p{On 2026-11-23, with llvm-project \code{\verb~|f0e7941beee3~} and clang 23.1.3 for x86-64, \code{\verb~|ir2lean~} exported 27 of the 96 single-precision entrypoints of the math library of LLVM libc, none of the 88 half-precision ones and none of the 9 double-precision ones that were surveyed. Among the 27, the approximations of a real function are \code{\verb~|expf~}, \code{\verb~|cospif~} and \code{\verb~|sinpif~}; the others are exact operations of IEEE 754.}
\p{What each of the others needs is in [the work list](note-extraction-worklist), by group of constructs, with the order that makes entrypoints exportable soonest in [the generated details](note-extraction-details). Each group is a change to \code{\verb~|extract/~}, to \code{\verb~|LibcMath/IR/Syntax.lean~} and to the semantics and the interpreter together. Close this tree when the list is empty or when the maintainer decides which functions are in scope; open one problem per group when work on it starts.}
